      "kind": "item",
      "label": "The find and replace panel looks unstyled",
      "excerpt": "The find and replace panel looks unstyled",
      "text": "Good.  Make it come up with `Replace` mode shown.",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-16T23:03:47.312Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-16T23:24:08.088Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  ⌘F now opens the find bar with its Replace row showing, in the code pane, the Inspector's Code card and <code>&lt;spell-editor&gt;</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>The compiled pane, read only, still has no Replace row.</li>\n  <li>The chevron still folds it away.  Folded, it stays folded:  in every editor, other files, and after a reload, until the chevron or ⌥⌘F shows it again (kept with the editor's other preferences;  J59).</li>\n  <li>⌥⌘F opens it with the Replace row, as before.</li>\n</ul>",
          "commit": "4c62a5900"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-16T23:07:46.328Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "j45",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "P6: the root package.json keeps its dompurify 3.4.17 resolution: dompurify is still a dependency of its own; only the known-open entry, which was Monaco's pin, went.",
      "excerpt": "P6: the root package.json keeps its dompurify 3.4.17 resolution: dompurify is still a dependency of its own; only the known-open entry, which was Monaco's pin, went.",
      "text": "remove",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-16T23:15:25.075Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-16T23:26:16.830Z",
          "html": "<p>Removed.  The root package.json no longer pins dompurify:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>it now comes from its own range (^3.4.0):  3.4.18, one patch newer than the pin</li>\n<li><code>spell deps check</code> passes:  0 to fix, 0 deprecated;  its one advisory is the known-open one already listed, not dompurify's</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Merged into main (94a08f0).</p>",
          "commit": "94a08f07d"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-16T23:22:17.964Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "j47",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "P7: App UI's pictures (CodeMirrorEditor.png, InputEditor.png, OutputEditor.png) still show Monaco: yarn site:pictures needs a running editor, not run overnight; the pages' prose is true",
      "excerpt": "P7: App UI's pictures (CodeMirrorEditor.png, InputEditor.png, OutputEditor.png) still show Monaco: yarn site:pictures needs a running editor, not run overnight; the pages' prose is true",
      "text": "do it",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-16T23:15:50.128Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-16T23:26:19.124Z",
          "html": "<p>Done.  App UI's three pictures now show CodeMirror, not Monaco:  InputEditor, OutputEditor, CodeMirrorEditor (the pictures are in the reply on J47).</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The compiled code shows only in Debug's Program panel now (its JavaScript tab), so the picture script opens Debug on that tab before it draws those two.</li>\n<li>So OutputEditor and CodeMirrorEditor look the same:  the panel doesn't draw the old \"Javascript Output\" toolbar.  OutputEditor's docs page still mentions that toolbar.</li>\n<li>The other pictures the script draws weren't redrawn.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Merged into main (9cbfa37).</p>",
          "commit": "9cbfa37f4"
        }
      ],
